## New-defect check on the fix itself

- **No false positive on within-body backward jumps.** I hand-retargeted the `:jump` at pc 4 to pc 0 (a backward loop inside body 0). `register-image-defect` returned nil, and `body-liveness` converged without error.
- **Rule cannot be skipped.** `register-image-defect` runs `structural-rules` then `some` over `body-rules`, and `jump-scope-rule` is the second body rule, so it runs on any image that passes shape and body-scope checks.
- **No lookup hazard.** Both `get owner` calls are total because `target-bounds-rule` guarantees the target is in range and `body-scope-rule` guarantees every in-range pc has an owner.

